---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import RadioGroupDemo from "../../components/RadioGroupDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Radio Group"
  description="A set of radios where one value is chosen."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Radio Group</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A set of round buttons where only one can be on. Use it for a short list of
    choices, such as how often to send a digest or when an agent replies.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><RadioGroupDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Radio group usage"
      code={`import { Label } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/label";
import { RadioGroup, RadioGroupItem } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/radio-group";

<RadioGroup defaultValue="weekly" aria-label="Digest frequency">
  <Label>
    <RadioGroupItem value="daily" />
    Daily
  </Label>
  <Label>
    <RadioGroupItem value="weekly" />
    Weekly
  </Label>
  <Label>
    <RadioGroupItem value="never" disabled />
    Unavailable
  </Label>
</RadioGroup>

const [rule, setRule] = useState<"tag" | "every-message">("tag");

<RadioGroup
  value={rule}
  onValueChange={setRule}
  aria-labelledby="reply-legend"
  aria-describedby="reply-helper"
  aria-required
>
  <p id="reply-legend">When should it reply?</p>
  <p id="reply-helper">Slack starts this agent from its attached channels.</p>
  <Label>
    <RadioGroupItem value="tag" aria-describedby="tag-description" />
    When mentioned
  </Label>
  <p id="tag-description">Replies to a mention, then follows that thread.</p>
</RadioGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass <code>value</code> and <code>onValueChange</code> to control the group,
      or <code>defaultValue</code> to let it keep its own state. The group may hold
      a legend, helper, error, and other text beside its radios.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a labeled set of bordered rows with descriptions, a requirement
      marker, and an error, use <code>ChoiceGroup type="radio"</code> from
      <a href="/components/field/">Field</a>. It is built from these parts.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      There is one look and one size: a 16px circle with a 40 × 32px hit area. A
      checked radio fills with the primary color and shows a dot.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>RadioGroup</code> takes <code>value</code>,
      <code>defaultValue</code>, <code>onValueChange</code>,
      <code>disabled</code>, <code>readOnly</code>, <code>required</code>,
      <code>name</code>, and ARIA props such as <code>aria-label</code>,
      <code>aria-labelledby</code>, <code>aria-describedby</code>,
      <code>aria-required</code>, and <code>aria-invalid</code>. It lays out its
      children in a grid with an 8px gap; pass <code>className</code> to change that.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>RadioGroupItem</code> takes a <code>value</code>,
      <code>disabled</code>, <code>id</code>, and
      <code>aria-describedby</code>. Set <code>aria-invalid</code> to draw a danger
      ring; an unchecked invalid radio also gets a danger border. Both parts accept
      Base UI props and state functions for
      <code>className</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The group has <code>role="radiogroup"</code> and each item has
      <code>role="radio"</code> with <code>aria-checked</code>, plus a hidden
      input for forms. Tab moves focus to the checked radio. Arrow keys move to
      the next radio and select it, skipping disabled ones. Space selects the
      focused radio. A focused radio shows a 2px focus ring.
    </p>
    <p>
      Name the group with <code>aria-label</code> or
      <code>aria-labelledby</code>, and name each radio with a wrapping
      <code>Label</code>, a <code>Label htmlFor</code>, or
      <code>aria-label</code>. Color changes take 120ms and the dot scales in
      over 180ms; both stop when reduced motion is requested. In forced colors
      mode a checked radio is highlighted.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Off uses <code>--sprout-border</code> on <code>--sprout-surface</code>,
      and hover uses <code>--sprout-border-strong</code>. On uses
      <code>--sprout-primary</code> with a <code>--sprout-on-primary</code>
      dot, so the opt-in TulipFarm theme tints it green. Invalid uses
      <code>--sprout-danger</code>, and focus uses <code>--sprout-focus</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
